HeaderInclude
config/e2k/e2k-opts.h

march=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(e2k_arch) Var(e2k_arch) Init(3)
-march=elbrus-vN	Generate code for ISA version N (3 to 7).

Enum
Name(e2k_arch) Type(int)
Known E2K ISA versions (for use with the -march= option):

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_arch) String(elbrus-v3) Value(3)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_arch) String(elbrus-v4) Value(4)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_arch) String(elbrus-v5) Value(5)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_arch) String(elbrus-v6) Value(6)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_arch) String(elbrus-v7) Value(7)

mtune=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(e2k_tune) Var(e2k_tune) Init(0)
-mtune=CPU	Generate code for that CPU only, as lcc does: its ISA version, which overrides -march, __elbrus_<cpu>__, its timing generation (see -mlatency=), and objects marked to run on it alone (EF_E2K_INCOMPAT).

Enum
Name(e2k_tune) Type(int)
Known E2K CPUs (for use with the -mtune= option):

; lcc's CPU codes (__builtin_cpu_is, spec/abi/source-compat.md).
EnumValue
Enum(e2k_tune) String(elbrus-4c) Value(4)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_tune) String(elbrus-8c2) Value(8)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_tune) String(elbrus-12c) Value(9)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_tune) String(elbrus-16c) Value(10)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_tune) String(elbrus-2c3) Value(11)

mlatency=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(e2k_lat) Var(e2k_lat) Init(0)
-mlatency=GEN	Schedule for the latencies of that generation (v3 for v1 to v5, which share them, or v6, also used for v7); the default follows the ISA version.  Not an lcc option.

Enum
Name(e2k_lat) Type(int)
Timing generations (for use with the -mlatency= option):

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_lat) String(v3) Value(3)

EnumValue
Enum(e2k_lat) String(v6) Value(6)

mbundle
Target Var(e2k_bundle) Init(1)
Pack operations into wide instructions after scheduling (default).  With -mno-bundle every operation is its own wide instruction and gas picks the channel.

mnops
Target Var(e2k_nops) Init(1)
Pad the gap between a producer and its consumer with nop N when the scheduler knows the latency.

mdbl
Target Var(e2k_dbl) Init(0)
Emit setwd dbl = 1 (32-bit integer operations zero-extend) instead of lcc's dbl = 0.

mdam
Target Var(e2k_dam) Init(1)
Move loads above stores that may write the same memory, with lock and check loads (the DAM).

mpipeline
Target Var(e2k_pipeline) Init(1)
Software-pipeline innermost counted loops (modulo scheduling with rotating %b[] registers and a peeled prologue, as lcc does).

mrename-window
Target Var(e2k_rename_window) Init(1)
In a function that calls, keep register renaming to the window registers register allocation used, so that each call keeps fewer below its callee.

mrename-window-shallow
Target Var(e2k_rename_window_shallow) Init(1)
With -mrename-window-ratio, leave out calls to functions known to be leaves or to call only leaves.

mrename-window-ratio=
Target Joined UInteger Var(e2k_rename_window_ratio) Init(16)
With -mrename-window, let register renaming take any window register in a function whose hottest block runs more than this many times as often as its hottest call (0: never).

mcond-returns-calls
Target Var(e2k_cond_returns_calls) Init(1)
Make branches to a return block conditional returns in functions that call too, preparing the return in the branching block.

mms-fma
Target Var(e2k_ms_fma) Init(1)
Combine a multiply and the add or subtract that alone reads its product into one operation in loops known to run long, as the pipeliner takes them.

mms-apb-recur
Target Var(e2k_ms_apb_recur) Init(1)
Pipeline a loop that a recurrence holds to about one iteration when its other loads can read through array prefetch from arrays that likely come from memory.

mms-apb-spread
Target Var(e2k_ms_apb_spread) Init(1)
Spread the areas of array prefetch over both halves of its buffer, so that each gets more of it.

mms-carry-slots
Target Var(e2k_ms_carry_slots) Init(1)
Pipeline a reload of a spill slot that the loop stores as a copy of the stored value.

mms-shorten
Target Var(e2k_ms_shorten) Init(1)
Move a pipelined loop's operations to shorten its values' lifetimes when the ring can't hold them.

mms-one-stage
Target Var(e2k_ms_one_stage) Init(1)
Schedule a big loop that fills the machine about as long as one iteration takes one iteration a pass, without overlap.

mms-big-ii=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(e2k_ms_big_ii) Init(6)
Pipeline a loop of 200 operations or more at an II up to this many quarters of one unpipelined iteration.

mapb-type-align
Target Var(e2k_apb_type_align) Init(1)
On v3 and v4, read elements through array prefetch when their type is aligned, without proving the pointer's alignment.

mapb-beside-backward
Target Var(e2k_apb_beside_backward) Init(0)
On v3 and v4, use array prefetch also in a loop that reads another array backwards with plain loads.

mloop-ctpr2-free
Target Var(e2k_loop_ctpr2_free) Init(1)
Don't prepare a loop's back edge in %ctpr2 around a hardware loop, whose array prefetch needs it.

mapb-wide-unroll
Target Var(e2k_apb_wide_unroll) Init(1)
Unroll by two a loop that loads a line or more apart each iteration, so that array prefetch reads each copy's loads through an area of its own.

mapb-derived
Target Var(e2k_apb_derived) Init(1)
Read through array prefetch also the loads whose base register the loop derives from an induction register plus an invariant.

mhwloop-unspill
Target Var(e2k_hwloop_unspill_p) Init(1)
Count a loop whose counter register allocation spilled in a register free in the loop, loaded on the way in, so that it can become a hardware loop.

mpipeline-while
Target Var(e2k_pipeline_while) Init(1)
Software-pipeline innermost while loops of one block, or of two whose first one exits (the exits combined with landp), with speculative operations and the exit test in the last stage.

mclock-prologue
Target Var(e2k_ms_clock_prologue) Init(1)
Give a pipelined loop's prologue the cycles of its modulo schedule, in a block of its own.

malias-version
Target Var(e2k_alias_version) Init(1)
Version innermost loops whose arrays may overlap on a runtime test, with a copy that assumes they don't (as lcc does).

mav-split
Target Var(e2k_av_split_p) Init(1)
Split a loop after the iteration whose store writes an element the loop keeps in a register (PolyBench's floyd-warshall), so that neither part carries it.

mcond-loads
Target Var(e2k_cond_loads_p) Init(1)
In innermost loops, run loads that a branch skips always when the loop stores to the same memory on every path, so that the branch becomes a select.

malias-version-block
Target Var(e2k_alias_version_block) Init(1)
Version blocks outside loops whose loads follow stores through other pointers on a runtime test of the ranges, with a copy that assumes they don't overlap (as lcc does).

mfmul-add
Target Var(e2k_fmul_add) Init(0)
Use the combined operations fmul_add, fmul_sub and fmul_rsub for a multiply followed by an add or subtract (with -ffp-contract=fast).

mcontrol-spec
Target Var(e2k_control_spec) Init(1)
Let the scheduler move loads and integer operations above branches, as speculative operations (,sm).

mloop-ct
Target Var(e2k_loop_ct) Init(1)
Close innermost loops with ct through a CTPR prepared before the loop instead of ibranch.

mchannels
Target Var(e2k_channels) Init(1)
Choose the ALU channel of each operation, keeping consumers in their producers' cluster.

mprepare-branches
Target Var(e2k_prepare_br) Init(1)
Prepare every branch with a free CTPR (disp + ct) instead of ibranch.

mspec-rename
Target Var(e2k_spec_rename_p) Init(1)
Give values a block computes after a branch their own registers where that lets them move above the branch.

maddr-height
Target Var(e2k_addr_height_p) Init(1)
Rebuild addresses computed as chains so that the operand ready last is added last, by the access.

munpred-dam=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(e2k_unpred_dam) Init(1) IntegerRange(0, 2)
Which loads e2k_unpredicate_loads runs without their predicate the DAM may move above stores, with a check under the predicate: 0 none, 1 the pairs of a select, 2 all.

mms-est
Target Var(e2k_ms_est) Init(1)
Where the modulo scheduler's order by start within an iteration fails at an II, order by the earliest start at that II, carried dependences included.

mspec-fp
Target Var(e2k_spec_fp) Init(1)
Let FP operations run speculatively, as lcc's -fspec-fp (its default): every operation of a pipelined loop but its stores runs ahead, speculative (,sm).  With -mno-spec-fp no FP operation does, for programs that clear or unmask FP exceptions, whose speculative FP results would be diagnostic (SIGILL).

mspec-prune
Target Var(e2k_spec_prune_p) Init(1)
Print ,sm only on operations that may fail or may read a diagnostic value, not on every operation run ahead of its guard.

muncond-ct-cost
Target Var(e2k_uncond_ct_cost) Init(1)
Schedule an unconditional ct the whole 5 cycles after its disp, as it always waits for it.

mcond-latches
Target Var(e2k_cond_latches_p) Init(1)
Copy a block that jumps back to a loop's top into a block branching to it, under its condition, and branch to the top directly.

mhoist-inv
Target Var(e2k_hoist_inv_p) Init(1)
Move loop invariants that the middle end left in a loop onto its ways in, after register allocation.

mhoist-prepares
Target Var(e2k_hoist_prep_p) Init(1)
Prepare a branch at the end of a short extended block in the blocks before it, where its disp has time to finish.

mtail-dup-joins
Target Var(e2k_tail_dup_joins_p) Init(1)
Copy a small block that a conditional branch falls into, and that jumps also enter, for the jumps, so that it continues the branch's extended block.

mrotate-headers
Target Var(e2k_rotate_headers_p) Init(1)
Move a loop header's leading operations into the latches, before their exit test, and onto the ways in.

munpredicate-arms
Target Var(e2k_unpred_arms_p) Init(1)
Run integer operations that if-conversion put under a predicate before the compare, without it, when only operations under the same predicate read their result.

mring-setwd
Target Var(e2k_ring_setwd) Init(1)
In a function that calls, grow the window around each pipelined loop for its register ring (as lcc), instead of keeping the largest ring below the outgoing registers everywhere.

munpredicate-loads
Target Var(e2k_unpred_loads_p) Init(1)
Run loads that if-conversion put under a predicate speculatively without it, when only operations under the predicate read their result.

munpred-limit=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(e2k_unpred_limit) Init(1000000)
Unpredicate at most this many loads (debugging).

mmerge-chains
Target Var(e2k_merge_chains_p) Init(1)
Merge chains of branches to one place into one branch on the landp of their conditions, running the operations between them speculatively.

mrotate-preds
Target Var(e2k_rotate_preds) Init(1)
Give a pipelined while loop's predicates rotating names (setbp, abp), so that its exit test may span iterations and its kernel be shorter than 3 cycles.

mcond-returns
Target Var(e2k_cond_returns_p) Init(1)
In a function without calls, copy a small block that returns into the branches to it and return from there under their conditions.

mapb
Target Var(e2k_apb) Init(1)
Read the loads of pipelined counted loops through array prefetch.

mapb-force
Target Var(e2k_apb_force) Init(0)
Use array prefetch for every load that may (testing): also where it doesn't shorten the kernel of a loop not known to run long.

mapb-unknown-count
Target Var(e2k_apb_unknown) Init(1)
Use array prefetch in counted loops whose trip count is unknown, as lcc does; without it they are taken to be short.

mstaa
Target Var(e2k_staa) Init(1)
Store through the AAU (staa with incr) in pipelined counted loops, as lcc does.

mnarrow-ext
Target Var(e2k_narrow_ext_p) Init(1)
After register allocation, turn an extension whose result is only read in its low 32 bits into a 32-bit copy.

mlatch-copies
Target Var(e2k_latch_copies_p) Init(1)
Move register copies out of a loop's latch, before its exit test, so that the loop can be counted and pipelined.

mms-load-far=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(e2k_ms_load_far) Init(48)
In pipelined loops, read a load no recurrence goes through this many cycles after it issues (0: its latency), for several misses in flight.

mms-long
Target Var(e2k_ms_long) Init(1)
Pipeline a loop known to run long for any gain over one iteration's length.

mms-tbaa
Target Var(e2k_ms_tbaa) Init(1)
Leave out a pipelined loop's dependences from a store to a later load of a type that can't alias it (strict aliasing).

mms-fixed-regs
Target Var(e2k_ms_fixed) Init(1)
Keep the values of a pipelined loop that live no longer than its initiation interval in their own registers, outside the rotating ring.

mms-list-prologue
Target Var(e2k_ms_list_pro) Init(1)
List-schedule the prologues of pipelined loops instead of keeping the modulo schedule's times.

mdam-stores-late
Target Var(e2k_dam_stores_late) Init(1)
Place a pipelined loop's lock load and check before the stores the body has before them, which then take the rows the check leaves.

mdam-deep
Target Var(e2k_dam_deep) Init(1)
Limit a pipelined loop with a lock load by the stages from the lock to its check, which hold entries, not by all its stages.

mdam-far
Target Var(e2k_dam_far) Init(1)
Read a pipelined loop's lock load as far ahead as other far loads (-mms-load-far), its check near the stores it must follow, as lcc's histogram loops have it.

mdam-apb
Target Var(e2k_dam_apb) Init(1)
Read a pipelined loop with a lock load through array prefetch too, its compensation code going back to the kernel by an ibranch.

mav-rows
Target Var(e2k_av_rows) Init(1)
Version a loop for two references whose addresses differ by an amount the loop doesn't know, which the dependence test takes for one element (rows of one array, NPB FT's fftz2).

mms-fma-ii
Target Var(e2k_ms_fma_ii) Init(1)
In a pipelined loop not known to run long, combine multiplies with the adds after them only where that shortens the initiation interval.

maau-setup-war
Target Var(e2k_aau_setup_war) Init(1)
Let an ALU operation share the wide instruction of an AAU register write before it, as the next descriptor base into the temporary does.

mchain-offsets
Target Var(e2k_chain_offsets) Init(1)
Take a loop that advances a pointer by an offset loaded through it, from an element at a computed index, for a hash chain's walk (Lua's tables), which the pipeliner leaves alone.

mhoist-taken-loads
Target Var(e2k_hoist_taken_p) Init(1)
Run the loads that start a branch's taken successor above the branch, speculatively, where only that branch reaches it.
